{"item_id": "BM0368", "position": 368, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-007", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "answer <- qchisq(0.95, df = 4)", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": [], "note": "-2 ln(U) has a chi-squared distribution with 2 df, so the sum of two independent terms has a chi-squared distribution with 4 df."}
{"item_id": "BM0369", "position": 369, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-008", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "", "answer_expression": "pct_diff <- function(observed, baseline = 0.50) (observed - baseline) / baseline * 100", "test_inputs": [{"kind": "question_data", "code": "observed <- 0.60"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "observed <- c(0.45, 0.72, 0.38)"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "set.seed(2); observed <- runif(5)"}, {"kind": "edge", "code": "observed <- 0.50"}], "correct_options": [], "note": "Defines a one-line function where baseline defaults to 0.50; the tests supply observed win rates."}
{"item_id": "BM0370", "position": 370, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-009", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "value <- 260 / 119\nanswer <- if (value > 1.5) \"B\" else \"A\"", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": ["B"], "note": "Residual deviance divided by df is about 2.18, well above 1, which points to overdispersion."}
