{"item_id": "BM0372", "position": 372, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-011", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "answer <- 2.1 + (6.4 - 6)^2", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": [], "note": "MSE equals variance plus squared bias."}
{"item_id": "BM0373", "position": 373, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-012", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "x <- c(12.5, 13.1, 14.0, 15.2, 16.8, 17.5, 18.9, 20.1, 21.3, 22.7)\nlow <- head(x, -3)\nhigh <- tail(x, -3)\nanswer <- mean(low) - mean(high)", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": [], "note": "Runs the given code directly."}
{"item_id": "BM0374", "position": 374, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-013", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "", "answer_expression": "fact <- function(n) if (n <= 1) 1 else n * fact(n - 1)", "test_inputs": [{"kind": "question_data", "code": "n <- 5"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "n <- 10"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "n <- 3"}, {"kind": "edge", "code": "n <- 0"}], "correct_options": [], "note": "One-line recursive definition; the tests supply values of n."}
{"item_id": "BM1329", "position": 375, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-014", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "x <- c(5, 8, 11); y <- c(2, 6, 10)\nall <- c(x, y)\ncmb <- combn(6, 3)\nd <- apply(cmb, 2, function(i) mean(all[i]) - mean(all[-i]))\nobs <- mean(x) - mean(y)\nanswer <- mean(d >= obs - 1e-9)", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": [], "note": "Lists all 20 ways to split the six values into two groups of 3 and counts differences at least as large as the observed one."}
{"item_id": "BM1331", "position": 376, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-015", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "t1 <- (10.1 - 10) / (0.2 / sqrt(25)); p1 <- 2 * pt(-abs(t1), 24)\nt2 <- (10.1 - 10) / (0.2 / sqrt(100)); p2 <- 2 * pt(-abs(t2), 99)\nvalue <- c(p1 = p1, p2 = p2)\nanswer <- if (p2 < p1) \"D\" else if (abs(p2 - p1) < 1e-12) \"B\" else \"A\"", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": ["D"], "note": "Computes both t-test p-values; the larger n gives a smaller standard error and so a smaller p-value."}
{"item_id": "BM1336", "position": 377, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-016", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "b1 <- 18.92; b2 <- 0.0542\nvalue <- 2 * b2\nanswer <- if (b2 > 0 && abs(value - 0.1084) < 1e-10) \"A\" else \"C\"", "answer_expression": "", "test_inputs": [], "correct_options": ["A"], "note": "The derivative is b1 + 2*b2*density = 18.92 + 0.1084*density; b2 > 0, so the curve is convex and C is wrong."}
{"item_id": "BM0378", "position": 378, "batch": "2026-11-25_kc-c2_17", "anon_id": "M-17-017", "kind": "solve-compute", "role": "C2", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "status": "computed", "r_code": "", "answer_expression": "get_fit_stats <- function(mod) c(r2 = summary(mod)$r.squared, sigma = summary(mod)$sigma)", "test_inputs": [{"kind": "variation", "code": "mod <- lm(mpg ~ wt, data = mtcars)"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "set.seed(3); d <- data.frame(x1 = rnorm(50), x2 = rnorm(50)); d$y <- 1 + 2 * d$x1 - d$x2 + rnorm(50); mod <- lm(y ~ x1 + x2, data = d)"}, {"kind": "variation", "code": "mod <- lm(Sepal.Length ~ Species, data = iris)"}, {"kind": "edge", "code": "set.seed(4); d <- data.frame(y = rnorm(20)); mod <- lm(y ~ 1, data = d)"}], "correct_options": [], "note": "Pulls r.squared and sigma from summary.lm; the question gives no data, so the tests use built-in and simulated models."}
